config DRM_PARHELIA
	tristate "Matrox Parhelia"
	depends on DRM && PCI
	select DRM_GEM_VRAM_HELPER
	select DRM_GEM_DMA_HELPER
	select I2C
	select I2C_ALGOBIT
	select FW_LOADER
	select CRC32
	help
	  DRM driver for the Matrox Parhelia P-series (Parhelia-512, Parhelia8x,
	  Parhelia-LX and P690) graphics adapters.  It provides native KMS for
	  the primary display controller, VRAM GEM objects and a validated DMA
	  submission interface for the WARP 3D engine.

	  The same module contains an isolated, default-off clean-room bring-up
	  backend for M9/Phoenix device 102b:0540.  It does not share engine
	  packets or initialization with the P-series path.  m9_enable=1 exposes
	  its DMA32 GEM and validate-only render interface; m9_render_diag=1 is
	  additionally required for the kernel-owned writeback-fence diagnostic.
	  Requires the locally extracted parhelia/mtx*.bin resident firmware
	  files in /lib/firmware (also in the initramfs for early loading).

	  If compiled as a module, it will be called parhelia.
